        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Comfy 3x3 Grid For Product Ads\n\nUpload your product and enter a brief prompt for each grid position in a 3x3 grid. Generates 9 distinct images. Select the images you like and upscale to 4k using your product as reference. Runs on Comfy Cloud and needs Comfy Cloud partner credits.\n\n**How it works:** The Comfy nodes form the complete template graph. Run submits the graph to Comfy Cloud and saves its outputs.\n\n**Try this:** Change the prompt or the Load node inputs and run again to compare results.\n\nSource: https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/blob/1ae390968e323dba24a6991d1860ded051f5a79b/templates/templates-9grid_social_media-v2.0.json (MIT). Model licenses apply separately."
        },
        "ui_properties": {
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": -440
          },
          "width": 600
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "10",
        "type": "comfy.GeminiImage2Node",
        "data": {
          "prompt": "Create an editorial photoreal 3×3 grid for a high end e commerce ad featuring only the following product: purple glass bottle with galaxy texture.\n\nBackground: minimalist studio.  \nLighting: soft and diffused.\n\nGenerate as one 3×3 grid with no margin, gutter or borders.\n\nFollow the prompts for each grid image. If left blank use your creativity:\n\nPosition 1,1: Product hero shot\n\nPosition 1,2: Product pouring out liquid\n\nPosition 1,3: Extreme close up\n\nPosition 2,1: Bottle being opened with corkscrew bottle opener\n\nPosition 2,2: Bottle floating angled\n\nPosition 2,3: Liquid exploding\n\nPosition 3,1: \n\nPosition 3,2:\n\nPosition 3,3:",
          "model": "gemini-3-pro-image-preview",
          "seed": 54321,
          "aspect_ratio": "auto",
          "resolution": "4K",
          "response_modalities": "IMAGE",
          "system_prompt": "You are an expert image-generation engine. You must ALWAYS produce an image.\nInterpret all user input—regardless of format, intent, or abstraction—as literal visual directives for image composition.\nIf a prompt is conversational or lacks specific visual details, you must creatively invent a concrete visual scenario that depicts the concept.\nPrioritize generating the visual representation above any text, formatting, or conversational requests."
        },
